  faqs: [
    { question: "I don't know where to begin looking for a tutor in Bhagalpur. What's the first step?", answer: "Just describe the situation: programme or board, subject, level, exam session. We use that to put together a shortlist, since no Bhagalpur school teaches IB or IGCSE and location was never going to be the deciding factor anyway. Once a lesson time is settled around your evening, a free trial comes first, and we adjust if it isn't the right match." },
    { question: "Can Bhagalpur families access tutoring for both Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE?", answer: "Both, and both delivered online. A Cambridge student is matched against their precise code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended for example, while an Edexcel student is matched against their specification and Foundation or Higher tier, each using that board's own past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Is a home visit ever part of the picture in Bhagalpur?", answer: "It isn't. IB Gram's in-person work stops at Gurugram and a handful of Delhi NCR pockets, nowhere near Bhagalpur. What happens instead is a live online lesson, video call, shared screen, and that's genuinely how the tuition gets delivered here, not a workaround for something we can't actually provide." },
    { question: "How much should a family in Bhagalpur expect to pay?", answer: "That depends on programme and level, the subject itself, how long sessions run, and how recently a tutor has taught this exact syllabus; we confirm a number for your match before the trial starts. HL Diploma work typically costs more than MYP or IGCSE Core support. Online delivery means no travel charge, and nothing is billed as a fixed-term package." },
    { question: "Has any school in or around Bhagalpur actually started teaching IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not as far as any directory we've checked shows, in Bhagalpur or in Patna. Families set on a school rather than a tutor generally look at boarding options in Kolkata, Delhi NCR, or the Mussoorie-Dehradun belt, home to Woodstock School's long-running IB MYP and Diploma Programme." },
    { question: "Does the free trial come with any catch?", answer: "None that we're aware of. A real topic from the actual syllabus, worked through live online, no charge, no strings attached to continuing afterward. What follows is a short plan for the first month, and only then do you decide whether to proceed, adjust something, or look at a different tutor." },
    { question: "Would a tutor ever write part of an Internal Assessment for my child?", answer: "That's a firm no, every time it comes up. The legitimate help looks different: shaping a research question into something workable, unpacking what an assessment criterion is really asking for, checking over a data-collection plan, giving straight feedback on a draft. Producing any of the assessed content itself would breach IB integrity rules outright." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects get requested most by Bhagalpur-linked families?", answer: "Both Maths routes, Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, at HL and SL, top the list, with Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science close behind, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance alongside whatever else a student carries." },
    { question: "Is this only for Diploma students, or can younger IB students get help too?", answer: "It spans the full continuum. MYP requests generally centre on criterion-based work in the sciences and Individuals and Societies, plus staying on top of a Personal Project journal. PYP requests are lighter touch: reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research, delivered in short sessions suited to a younger child." },
    { question: "Can an online lesson genuinely replace a tutor sitting in the room?", answer: "For a Bhagalpur student, it arguably does the job better, since the alternative, a local specialist in this exact syllabus, doesn't really exist to begin with, and no in-person option is on offer here in any case. Between a shared screen, live worked examples and sessions saved for later review, very little actually goes missing, and the search opens up to specialists across the country instead of just the neighbourhood." },
    { question: "How thoroughly are tutors actually vetted before we're introduced?", answer: "The focus is on what they've taught recently, at the precise level in question, and their track record supervising Internal Assessments, rather than a general credential on paper. Because Bhagalpur has no local IB or IGCSE school to benchmark against, we deliberately seek out tutors with recent, hands-on experience elsewhere in the country." },
    { question: "Is there an ideal age or stage to bring in a tutor?", answer: "Right at the start of the course tends to work best, Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE, leaving time to close gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all converge. A later start is still worthwhile, just with the plan trimmed down to the highest-impact topics and past papers." },
    { question: "How difficult is switching from the Bihar Board or CBSE into IB or IGCSE?", answer: "It comes up constantly among families here, for the obvious reason that no local school offers either curriculum from day one. The real adjustment usually isn't the content but the question style: terms like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need to be taught explicitly, and beginning that work over the preceding summer smooths out the first term considerably." },
    { question: "Do sessions run on weekends, or strictly on weekday evenings?", answer: "Either works. Weekday evenings tend to suit once school and coaching classes are done for the day, and weekend mornings work well when the household has more breathing room. Scheduling accounts for Bhagalpur's summer heat, the chance of monsoon disruption near the Ganga, and breaks like Chhath rather than working around them as an afterthought." },
    { question: "What's the process if a tutor turns out to be a poor match for my child?", answer: "Flag it, and a replacement gets found. Regular check-ins every few weeks exist specifically to surface this early, and there's no contract obligating anyone to continue with a match that isn't working. Pausing or stopping altogether is also always on the table, with nothing owed either way." },
    { question: "Is there any formal connection between IB Gram and a school in Bhagalpur, or the IB itself?", answer: "None at all. Every school referenced on this page, along with the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education, and Pearson Edexcel, is entirely separate from IB Gram. Naming them simply shows where a genuine curriculum option exists, and tutoring follows whichever school calendar and published syllabus actually applies." },
  ],

